{
  "version": 8,
  "dashboardId": "tracking_golden",
  "title": "Tracking — Golden Signals",
  "description": "Delivery state and golden signals for the Tracking service. Combines the CloudWatch metrics it publishes (PromQL panels) with its per-request log line (SQL panels). That request log was added specifically so this dashboard could carry request rate, latency and top routes — before it, Tracking was the only HTTP service emitting no http_route or duration_ms at all.",
  "role": "",
  "owner": "3MRAI",
  "created": "2026-08-13T00:00:00Z",
  "tabs": [
    {
      "tabId": "default",
      "name": "Delivery & Traffic",
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": "tracking_orders_by_status",
          "type": "line",
          "title": "Orders — finished vs in progress",
          "description": "DELIVERED is the state machine's terminal status, so 'finished' is the domain's own invariant. One tracking per order (uq_tracking_order_id), so these counts are order counts. A gauge, hence max() — sum() would add every sample in the window and report a multiple of the truth.",
          "config": {
            "show_legends": true,
            "decimals": 0
          },
          "queryType": "promql",
          "queries": [
            {
              "query": "max by (status) (amazonaws_com_3mrai_orders_by_tracking_status_total{status!=\"\"})",
              "customQuery": true,
              "fields": {
                "stream": "amazonaws_com_3mrai_orders_by_tracking_status_total",
                "stream_type": "metrics",
                "x": [],
                "y": [],
                "z": [],
                "breakdown": [],
                "filter": {
                  "filterType": "group",
                  "logicalOperator": "AND",
                  "conditions": []
                }
              },
              "config": {
                "promql_legend": "{status}",
                "layer_type": "scatter",
                "weight_fixed": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 96,
            "h": 15,
            "i": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tracking_total_tracked",
          "type": "line",
          "title": "Orders with a tracking record",
          "description": "DELIVERED + IN_PROGRESS — every order Tracking knows about. Compare against orders_total on the Business Metrics dashboard: the difference is orders whose init-tracking call failed, a failure mode Orders accepts deliberately rather than failing the order. Normally zero.",
          "config": {
            "show_legends": false,
            "decimals": 0
          },
          "queryType": "promql",
          "queries": [
            {
              "query": "sum(amazonaws_com_3mrai_orders_by_tracking_status_total)",
              "customQuery": true,
              "fields": {
                "stream": "amazonaws_com_3mrai_orders_by_tracking_status_total",
                "stream_type": "metrics",
                "x": [],
                "y": [],
                "z": [],
                "breakdown": [],
                "filter": {
                  "filterType": "group",
                  "logicalOperator": "AND",
                  "conditions": []
                }
              },
              "config": {
                "promql_legend": "tracked orders",
                "layer_type": "scatter",
                "weight_fixed": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": {
            "x": 96,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 96,
            "h": 15,
            "i": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tracking_http_errors",
          "type": "line",
          "title": "HTTP errors by class",
          "description": "4xx/5xx only. The 5xx series is captured through an explicit exception branch in the ASGI middleware: Starlette's ServerErrorMiddleware sits outside every add_middleware layer, so an unhandled exception's 500 never reaches a send wrapper and would otherwise go uncounted (see docs/lessons/2026-08-12-server-error-middleware-outside-pure-asgi-middleware.md).",
          "config": {
            "show_legends": true,
            "decimals": 0
          },
          "queryType": "promql",
          "queries": [
            {
              "query": "sum by (statusclass) (amazonaws_com_3mrai_http_errors_total{service=\"tracking\",statusclass!=\"\"})",
              "customQuery": true,
              "fields": {
                "stream": "amazonaws_com_3mrai_http_errors_total",
                "stream_type": "metrics",
                "x": [],
                "y": [],
                "z": [],
                "breakdown": [],
                "filter": {
                  "filterType": "group",
                  "logicalOperator": "AND",
                  "conditions": []
                }
              },
              "config": {
                "promql_legend": "{statusclass}",
                "layer_type": "scatter",
                "weight_fixed": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 15,
            "w": 192,
            "h": 15,
            "i": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tracking_req_rate",
          "type": "line",
          "title": "Request rate",
          "description": "Requests per interval. Now possible because the service emits a per-request log line; before that, http_route was absent from every record.",
          "config": {
            "show_legends": false,
            "decimals": 0
          },
          "queryType": "sql",
          "queries": [
            {
              "query": "SELECT histogram(_timestamp) AS x_axis_1, COUNT(*) AS y_axis_1 FROM logs WHERE service_name = 'tracking' AND http_route IS NOT NULL GROUP BY x_axis_1",
              "customQuery": true,
              "fields": {
                "stream": "logs",
                "stream_type": "logs",
                "x": [
                  {
                    "label": "time",
                    "alias": "x_axis_1",
                    "column": "x_axis_1",
                    "color": null,
                    "isDerived": true,
                    "havingConditions": [],
                    "treatAsNonTimestamp": true
                  }
                ],
                "y": [
                  {
                    "label": "requests",
                    "alias": "y_axis_1",
                    "column": "y_axis_1",
                    "color": "#2196f3",
                    "isDerived": true,
                    "havingConditions": [],
                    "treatAsNonTimestamp": true
                  }
                ],
                "z": [],
                "breakdown": [],
                "filter": {
                  "filterType": "group",
                  "logicalOperator": "AND",
                  "conditions": []
                }
              },
              "config": {
                "promql_legend": "",
                "layer_type": "scatter",
                "weight_fixed": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 30,
            "w": 96,
            "h": 15,
            "i": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tracking_latency_pctl",
          "type": "line",
          "title": "Latency percentiles",
          "description": "p50/p95/p99 of request duration. A p99 climbing while p50 stays flat points at a slow dependency on a subset of requests rather than a general slowdown.",
          "config": {
            "show_legends": true,
            "decimals": 0
          },
          "queryType": "sql",
          "queries": [
            {
              "query": "SELECT histogram(_timestamp) AS x_axis_1, approx_percentile_cont(duration_ms, 0.5) AS y_axis_1, approx_percentile_cont(duration_ms, 0.95) AS y_axis_2, approx_percentile_cont(duration_ms, 0.99) AS y_axis_3 FROM logs WHERE service_name = 'tracking' AND duration_ms IS NOT NULL GROUP BY x_axis_1",
              "customQuery": true,
              "fields": {
                "stream": "logs",
                "stream_type": "logs",
                "x": [
                  {
                    "label": "time",
                    "alias": "x_axis_1",
                    "column": "x_axis_1",
                    "color": null,
                    "isDerived": true,
                    "havingConditions": [],
                    "treatAsNonTimestamp": true
                  }
                ],
                "y": [
                  {
                    "label": "p50",
                    "alias": "y_axis_1",
                    "column": "y_axis_1",
                    "color": "#4caf50",
                    "isDerived": true,
                    "havingConditions": [],
                    "treatAsNonTimestamp": true
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "p95",
                    "alias": "y_axis_2",
                    "column": "y_axis_2",
                    "color": "#ff9800",
                    "isDerived": true,
                    "havingConditions": [],
                    "treatAsNonTimestamp": true
                  },
                  {
                    "label": "p99",
                    "alias": "y_axis_3",
                    "column": "y_axis_3",
                    "color": "#f44336",
                    "isDerived": true,
                    "havingConditions": [],
                    "treatAsNonTimestamp": true
                  }
                ],
                "z": [],
                "breakdown": [],
                "filter": {
                  "filterType": "group",
                  "logicalOperator": "AND",
                  "conditions": []
                }
              },
              "config": {
                "promql_legend": "",
                "layer_type": "scatter",
                "weight_fixed": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": {
            "x": 96,
            "y": 30,
            "w": 96,
            "h": 15,
            "i": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tracking_top_routes",
          "type": "bar",
          "title": "Top routes",
          "description": "Busiest routes. http_route is the TEMPLATE (/v1/trackings/{order_id}), never the concrete id — otherwise every order would become its own route and this panel would be useless.",
          "config": {
